abstract: >-
  The Agent Execution Integrity Benchmark (AEIB) v0.2.4 is a locally
  reproducible evaluation harness demonstrating that autonomous AI agents
  suffer duplicate mutations when suffering semantic drift during retry loops
  after a post-commit HTTP 504 transport severance. AEIB enforces a
  four-step boundary (state freeze, out-of-band authoritative probe,
  JCS + Ed25519 cryptographic receipt, and offline verification) to achieve
  zero observed duplicate debits across 50 deterministic fault trials.
  The release includes a versioned transport-to-disposition mapping contract,
  an explicit retry-policy vocabulary, a standalone offline verifier, and
  a live PostgreSQL integration suite. Status: locally executed and internally
  reproducible; external independent reproduction pending.
keywords:
